  "type": "manhwa",
  "description": "What does the \"Wu\" in Wuxia truly mean? It is the power to enforce one's chivalry—to wield justice not just for oneself, but to shape the world by sheer strength. And if that strength transcends the self, flows through others, and reaches to the ends of the world... Then that power is none other than divine. So what does it take for a mere human to ascend to such godhood? To reach the realm of the divine through martial might? Thus begins the epic tale of Pi Wol-ryeo, a warrior in search of that very answer—one forged in blood, will, and iron discipline.\n\n(Source: KakaoPage, translated)",
